      "changedAt": "2026-10-13T07:11:58.463Z",
      "sourceRunId": "0e3527fb-33b5-4d33-a1bf-7d4cf8bdbfdc",
      "changeType": "new",
      "active": true,
      "paragraphs": [
        "The Points Guy reports that Delta Air Lines has pushed back its nonstop Riyadh service to March 2027. According to that report, the delay follows attacks at the airport in Riyadh. The claim has not been verified against official Delta or airport materials in the evidence reviewed here.",
        "Because the revised date comes from editorial reporting rather than a confirmed airline schedule, the launch timing could shift again. Treat the March 2027 date as reported rather than final until Delta publishes updated schedule information."
      ],
      "keyPoints": [
        "Reported new launch date for Delta's nonstop Riyadh service: March 2027.",
        "The Points Guy attributes the delay to attacks at the Riyadh airport.",
        "No official confirmation of the change was present in the fetched evidence."
      ],
      "takeaway": "If you are planning a Riyadh trip, do not assume the Delta nonstop is running on its earlier schedule. Check Delta's own route and schedule information for the current launch date before booking connections."
    }
